WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.760
Welcome back to BBC Learning English!

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:03.780
I’m Sam

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.740
and today we’re looking at the difference between

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.130
come back and go back.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.680
They both mean to return,

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.769
but we use them differently.

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:19.160
We use come back when we return here.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.540
So, for example:

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.920
I am in the BBC building now.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.820
Tonight I will go home,

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.800
and tomorrow I will come back here

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.359
- like a full circle.

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:34.560
We use go back to mean that we return there.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.620
For example:

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:41.140
I am at work now, and tonight I will go back home.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.260
I am not at home now, but tonight I will go back

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.620
– half the circle

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.200
So, please come back to BBC Learning English

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.140
for more videos!

